# Console Debug Commands — Always JSON.stringify

When giving the user a browser/DevTools console snippet for debugging, tracing, or “paste the result back”:

## Required

- Prefer **`JSON.stringify(report)`** (optionally `JSON.stringify(report, null, 2)`) as the clipboard / copy payload.
- Prefer **`copy(JSON.stringify(...))`** when available so the user can paste a single string into chat.
- Do **not** rely on `console.log(object)` alone — Chrome DevTools collapses nested objects and expand-state does not survive paste into chat.

## Pattern

```js
const report = { /* flat, serializable fields */ };
console.log('[label]', JSON.stringify(report));
try {
  copy(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));
  console.log('Copied JSON to clipboard — paste it here');
} catch (_) {
  console.log(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));
}
```

## Avoid

- Asking the user to “expand the object in the console and screenshot”
- Logging Maps/Sets/DOM nodes without converting to plain JSON-safe data first
- Circular structures without a replacer / safe subset
